# BMAP format: bumpInstName bumpCellType x y portName netName
# Unlike DEF, BMAP x/y coordinates are written directly in microns.
# portName is the chiplet boundary terminal (dbBTerm).
# netName is the chiplet's internal dbNet.
bump_clk BUMP 15.0 17.0 clk clk
bump_d BUMP 15.0 19.0 d d
bump_q BUMP 19.0 19.0 q q
# Place the VDD bump on the metal5 VDD rail at (5 um, 6.4 um).
# VDD appears twice because the port and net are different objects with the same name.
bump_vdd BUMP 5.0 6.4 VDD VDD
# Place the VSS bump at (15 um, 5 um) and connect VSS dbBTerm to VSS dbNet.
# VSS appears twice because the port and net are different objects with the same name.
bump_vss BUMP 15.0 5.0 VSS VSS

